{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And here, in every shelamim offering, the right thigh belongs to the priest, and in the shelamim of a nazirite, the priest receives the thigh and the arm — which are the hand and the leg. But in the ram of ordination, the thigh was placed upon the altar. For although an ordinary offerer gives the thigh — which is with the leg — to the priest who enters within the partition of the ordinary offerer, the nazirite gives also the arm, which is the hand, as one surrendering to the priest the activity of his hands that until now had been directed to consecration to HaShem. But in the ordination offering, which was a sacrifice that qualified the priest to enter within, the thigh was placed upon the altar."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:35:55.699016903Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}